{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Day 31 — Probability refresh\n","Objectives:\n","- Distributions (Bernoulli, Binomial, Normal).\n","- Law of large numbers via simulation.\n","- Bayes basics (intuitive).\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["import numpy as np, matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","rng = np.random.default_rng(42)\n","# Bernoulli trials\n","p=0.6\n","x = rng.binomial(n=1, p=p, size=10_000)\n","x.mean()  # ~0.6\n","# LLN\n","cum_mean = np.cumsum(x) / (np.arange(len(x))+1)\n","plt.plot(cum_mean); plt.axhline(p,color='r'); plt.title('Convergence to p'); plt.show()\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Exercises\n","1) Simulate Binomial(n=10,p=0.3) 10000 times and plot histogram.\n","2) Generate Normal(0,1), compute mean/var, and overlay PDF using scipy if available.\n","3) Bayes: If test sensitivity=0.95, specificity=0.9, prevalence=1%, compute P(disease|positive).\n"]}]}
